# [UCP] U3 -- THE CHARACTER-STEPPED DFA over ILL-FORMED UTF-8
# (ucp_design.md §3.5): a byte that does not decode is one ill-formed
# character, in no set and not a word character, forward, in the
# reverse walk's step back, in the seeds and in the retry. Same patterns
# as tests/ucp/island.rxt; subjects mix well-formed characters with stray
# continuations, truncated leads, 0xFF, overlongs, surrogates and
# > U+10FFFF, plus hand subjects with a bad byte where each walk reads
# one, every startpos just after a bad byte, and `mg` counts.
#
# oracle-options: UTF|UCP|MIU
# ORACLE: libpcre2 10.46 2025-08-27 under PCRE2_UTF|PCRE2_UCP|PCRE2_MATCH_INVALID_UTF
# (pcrec's ruled `-e utf8` semantics), GENERATED by
# tests/ucp/gen_island_rxt.py, re-checked by its --verify mode
# (run_ucp_tests.sh §5).
#
# LEFT OUT: 21 cell(s) where pcrec's answer DIFFERS from PCRE2's, each an
# empty match beside an ill-formed byte (match_api.md §9.5's documented
# divergence, inherited from the byte machines; known_issues.md). Every
# other such cell is written, since it agrees:
#   (*UCP)\b\w*   ms 9 "\xc7\x85\xc2\xb7\xc3\xa9 foo\xf0\x9d\x9f\x98\xbf" 14 14
#   (*UCP)\b(?:|\w+)   mg "\xce\xb1\xff\xce\xb2" 7
#   (*UCP)\b(?:|\w+)   mg "\xc0\x80\xc3\xa9 foo\xbf\xce\xa9" 7
#   (*UCP)\b(?:|\w+)   mg "\xcc\x81\xc3\xf0\x9f\xce\xa9" 7
#   (*UCP)\b(?:|\w+)   mg "\xc7\x85.\xc3o\xc3\xa9" 7
#   (*UCP)\b\w*?   mg "foo\x80" 3
#   (*UCP)\b\w*?   mg "ab\x80cd" 7
#   (*UCP)\b\w*?   mg "\xce\xb1\xff\xce\xb2" 7
#   (*UCP)\b\w*?   ms 5 "\xce\xa9\xe6\x97\xa5\xc3\xa9\xbf\xc7\x85" 7 7
#   (*UCP)\b\w*?   mg "\xce\xa9\xe6\x97\xa5\xc3\xa9\xbf\xc7\x85" 7
#   (*UCP)\b   mg "foo\x80" 2
#   (*UCP)\b   mg "ab\x80cd" 4
#   (*UCP)\b   mg "\xc3\xa9\x80\xc3\xa9" 4
#   (*UCP)\b   mg "a\xbf\xbfb" 4
#   (*UCP)\b   mg "\x80 \xc2\xce\xa9\x80\xc3\xa9 foo" 6
#   (*UCP)\B   mg "\xffab cd\xc3" 3
#   (*UCP)\B   mg "\xe6\x97foo\xe6\x97" 3
#   (*UCP)\B   mg " \xf0\x9d\x9f\x98\xf4\x90\x80\x80\xff" 1
#   (*UCP)\B   mg "\xf4\x90\x80\x80\xf0\x9f\x98\x80\xcc\x81" 3
#   (*UCP)\B   ns 3 "foo\xf4\x90\x80\x80"
#   (*UCP)\B   mg "foo\xf4\x90\x80\x80" 2

